  "details": "Problem Statement\n\nVRChat's global community faces significant language barriers:\n\nLanguage isolation - speakers cluster in language-specific worlds only\n\nDiscovery difficulty - no way to find instances where your language is spoken\n\nMissed connections - users avoid public instances due to language uncertainty\n\nRegional segregation - communities remain separated instead of mixing naturally\n\nProposed Solution\n\nAdd language indicators to instance listings:\n\nVisual language tags next to server region indicators\n\nInstance creator language preference shown in world browser\n\nOptional language filter in instance search\n\nReal-time language detection based on current users (optional)\n\nImplementation Options\n\nCreator-set default: Instance creator selects primary language when launching\n\nAuto-detection: System suggests language based on user profiles in instance\n\nUser declaration: Players can mark their preferred language in instances\n\nHybrid approach: Combine creator intent with active user languages\n\nBenefits\n\nGlobal inclusion: All languages get visibility across all worlds\n\nNatural mixing: Language speakers spread beyond dedicated worlds\n\nEasier discovery: Find your language community in any game mode\n\nCultural exchange: Encourages cross-cultural interaction\n\nRetention improvement: New users find welcoming language communities faster\n\nUI Design Suggestion\n\nSimple flag icons or language codes (PT, ES, EN, JP, etc.) displayed alongside region indicators in instance listings.\n\nThis feature transforms VRChat from language-segregated communities into a truly international platform.",
